# Next.js Client Conventions

Applies to `client/`.

## Components

- **PascalCase** filenames: `MeetingResults.tsx`, `ConfirmationModal.tsx`.
- **One component per file**; default export or named export for the primary component.
- Presentational components must not contain business rules — use hooks or `lib/` helpers.

## Hooks

- Prefix with `use`: `useAuth.ts`.
- Custom hooks encapsulate data fetching, form state, and side effects.
- Reusable hooks live in `client/src/hooks/`; component-specific hooks may colocate with the component.

## Types and API

- UI and API consumer types live in `client/src/types/` (e.g. `meeting.ts`).
- Keep types aligned with server `dto/` and `interfaces/`; do not redefine divergent contract shapes.
- HTTP calls belong in `client/src/lib/api/` (e.g. `meetings.api.ts`, `auth.ts`).
- Use the shared axios instance from `client/src/lib/axios.ts`.

## Enums and constants

- Repeated domain strings (roles, statuses, auth error codes, redirect query values) belong in a **string enum** in `client/src/types/`, not inline literals.
- Compare with `UserRole.Admin`, `MeetingStatus.Completed`, etc. — never `'ADMIN'` or `'COMPLETED'` scattered in pages/hooks.
- Enum string values must match the server/API exactly. When the server adds a value, update the client enum in the same change when possible.
- App-only constants that are not domain enums (e.g. localStorage keys) may be `export const` in the same types module.

## Layout (from README)

```
client/src/
├── app/           # App Router pages & layouts
├── components/    # Shared UI (PascalCase)
├── hooks/         # useX hooks
├── lib/           # axios, api clients, auth helpers
├── providers/     # QueryProvider, AuthProvider, etc.
└── types/         # TypeScript interfaces
```
